### 7. ⚠️ MEDIUM: Missing CORS Configuration (OWASP A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration)

**Issue:** No CORS policy defined. Application will use permissive defaults, allowing any origin to access the API.

**Risk:** 
- Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
- Unauthorized cross-origin requests
- Sensitive data accessible from any website

**Recommendation:**
```javascript
const cors = require('cors');

// Restrictive CORS configuration
const corsOptions = {
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['https://example.com'],
  credentials: true,
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  maxAge: 3600, // 1 hour
};

app.use(cors(corsOptions));

// Add CSRF protection for state-changing operations
const csrfProtection = require('csurf');
const cookieParser = require('cookie-parser');

app.use(cookieParser());
app.use(csrfProtection({ cookie: true }));

// For POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints
app.post('/api/users', csrfProtection, (req, res) => {
  // CSRF token is automatically validated
});
```

**Implementation:**
```bash
npm install cors csurf cookie-parser
```

**Environment Configuration (.env):**
```
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://app.example.com
```

