### 9. ⚠️ MEDIUM: No HTTPS/TLS Configuration

**Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM  
**Category:** CWE-295 (Improper Certificate Validation), OWASP A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures

**Issue:**
Application listens only on HTTP (port 3000), not HTTPS. All traffic is unencrypted and vulnerable to man-in-the-middle attacks.

**Recommendations:**

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');
const app = express();

// Force HTTPS redirect (if behind reverse proxy)
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.header('x-forwarded-proto') !== 'https' && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
    res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
  } else {
    next();
  }
});

// If running standalone (not behind reverse proxy):
const options = {
  key: fs.readFileSync('/path/to/private-key.pem'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync('/path/to/certificate.pem')
};

https.createServer(options, app).listen(443, () => {
  console.log('Secure server running on port 443');
});

app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
});
```

