## A01:2021 - Broken Access Control

### VULNERABLE CODE
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});

app.get('/admin/settings', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ apiKey: 'secret-key', database: 'prod-db' });
});
```

**Issues:**
- No authentication - anyone can access
- No authorization - no role checks
- Sensitive data exposed to public
- Admin endpoints accessible to all

**Attack Example:**
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/admin/settings
# Returns: { "apiKey": "secret-key", "database": "prod-db" }
```

### SECURE CODE
```javascript
const authenticate = (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token required' });

  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    next();
  } catch {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
  }
};

const authorize = (roles) => (req, res, next) => {
  if (!roles.includes(req.user.role)) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
  }
  next();
};

app.get('/users', authenticate, authorize(['admin', 'user']), (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob' },
  ]);
});

app.get('/admin/settings', authenticate, authorize(['admin']), (req, res) => {
  res.json({ setting: 'value' });
});
```

**Benefits:**
- Requires valid JWT token
- Checks user role/permissions
- Sensitive data only for authorized users
- Admin endpoints restricted to admins

