134	### 3. ❌ **A05:2021 – Broken Authentication** (CRITICAL)
135	
136	**Issue:** The application has no authentication mechanism at all.
137	
138	**Vulnerabilities:**
139	- No user login functionality
140	- No session management
141	- No token-based authentication (JWT, OAuth)
142	- No password storage mechanism
143	- No account lockout protection
144	- No 2FA support
145	
146	**Recommendations:**
147	
148	1. **Implement JWT Authentication:**
149	```javascript
150	const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
151	const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');
152	require('dotenv').config();
153	
154	// Login endpoint
155	app.post('/login', async (req, res) => {
156	  const { email, password } = req.body;
157	  
158	  // Input validation
159	  if (!email || !password) {
160	    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Email and password required' });
161	  }
162	  
163	  // Fetch user from database (example)
164	  const user = await db.findUserByEmail(email);
165	  if (!user) {
166	    // Use generic error to prevent user enumeration
167	    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid credentials' });
168	  }
169	  
170	  // Compare passwords
171	  const isValid = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.passwordHash);
172	  if (!isValid) {
173	    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Invalid credentials' });
174	  }
175	  
176	  // Generate JWT
177	  const token = jwt.sign(
178	    { userId: user.id, email: user.email, role: user.role },
179	    process.env.JWT_SECRET,
180	    { expiresIn: '1h' }
181	  );
182	  
183	  res.json({ token, expiresIn: 3600 });
184	});
185	```
186	
187	2. **Add Logout (Token Blacklist):**
188	```javascript
189	const tokenBlacklist = new Set();
190	
191	app.post('/logout', authenticate, (req, res) => {
192	  const token = req.headers.authorization.split(' ')[1];
193	  tokenBlacklist.add(token);
194	  res.json({ success: true });
195	});
196	
197	// Update authenticate middleware to check blacklist
198	const authenticate = (req, res, next) => {
199	  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
200	  if (!token || tokenBlacklist.has(token)) {
201	    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
202	  }
203	  // ... rest of logic
204	};
205	```
